<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Cost Analysis</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ B.4 Cost Analysis ‣ Appendix B More Experimental Details Results ‣ ParamMem: Augmenting Language Agents with Parametric Reflective Memory" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> reports prompt/completion tokens and costs using Llama-3.1-8B.
Costs are computed with TogetherAI pricing as of Aug 20, 2025 ($0.18 per million tokens).
We can see that Model-based Reflection (CoT) is highly efficient, achieving strong accuracy with far fewer tokens than reflection-heavy methods like DoT-bank.
By contrast, 
<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:5.3pt;height:6.2pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,-0.0pt) scale(1.0,1.0) ;">
<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">P</span></span>
</span></span><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">aram
<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:5.3pt;height:6.2pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,-0.0pt) scale(1.0,1.0) ;">
<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">A</span>
</span></span>gent</span> delivers the best results on both HumanEval and HotpotQA, at higher but still moderate cost, this highlights the advantages of incorporating various forms of memory modules.</p>
</div>
